# TypeScript style

No `class` in new code (including `extends Error`). Functional style with dependency injection as **functions that return functions**:

```typescript
export const createBus = (deps: BusDeps) => (name: string, options = {}) => {
  return { call, subscribe, method, close };
};
export const openBus = createBus(defaultDeps);
```

- Deps (native addon, timers, clock, other services) enter at the outer level so tests can fake them.
- Errors: factory function + type guard, not error subclasses.
- `defineElement` is the allowed exception for custom elements (one class in the kit).
- Package boundaries: `@webos/api` (no DOM) ← `@webos/ui-kit` ← `@gachlab/app-*`. Enforce with `tools/check-layers.mjs`, not greps that cannot fire.
- Our app ids: `com.gachlab.app.*`; use `aliases` for HP ids when replacing a system app.
